extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 109-111 (cache p109-p111, page_offset 0). The section heading on 109 reads ''Ojahee Cyborg O.C.C.'', the stat block on 111 reads ''Ojahee Borg O.C.C.'', and the text calls them O''borgs; the block''s name is stored. Printed 110 is a full-page illustration with no text. Printed 109 and 111 checked against a 200 dpi render; the OCR agreed on every number. No ojahee-borg class was in production on 2026-09-25. || XP: the Ojahee ''Borg, Ultra-Crazy and Arkhon Spectral Hunter ladder on printed 192, read off a render. Level 14 prints as starting at 400,000, the same figure level 13 ends on; that is a book slip, stored as printed (400000, still strictly rising), not corrected to 400,001. || RACE: race_restrictions only ojahee; the ojahee R.C.C. is drafted alongside this class and they ship together. || SUPERSEDES_RACE: set, and it is a judgement call. The book does not say the character stops being an Ojahee - it keeps its flesh and its supernatural strength, and the head or main body failing ''will kill the Ojahee''. But the O''borg''s printed main body, P.E. x3 +400 and +8 per level, replaces the Ojahee R.C.C.''s P.E. x5 +10 per level, and because the class is open to Ojahee only, without the flag the race''s pool would win EVERY pairing and the printed figure would never apply. With it, composition is right on every other count: the class states no attribute_dice, so the Ojahee dice stand; the race''s horror factor, P.P.E., bonuses and natural abilities are kept; the Megaversal Trooper (Ojahee) skill block the R.C.C. carries is replaced by this O.C.C.''s own list, which is what the book prints for an O''borg; starting_money is this class''s. Revisit if the ojahee R.C.C. ships without an mdc_base. || BODY: mdc_base holds the main body; the other locations are in the Partial Bionic Reconstruction ability. mdc_base is stated, so no men_of_arms line. || BONUSES: printed 111 gives COMBINED totals that include attribute and R.C.C. bonuses: +1 attack, +6 initiative, +2 parry, +4 pull punch, +4 save vs horror factor. The Ojahee R.C.C. prints one additional hand to hand attack at level one and +2 save vs horror factor, and a pairing sums both classes'' bonuses, so what is stored here is each total less the R.C.C.''s share: no attack (the R.C.C.''s one is the +1), initiative +6, parry +2, pull punch +4, horror factor +2. No attribute feeds these, because P.P. is the race''s roll. This assumes the ojahee R.C.C. stores its extra attack as combat attacks 1 and its +2 horror factor; if it does not, this block is short by the same amount. The +6 P.S. is stored as an attribute bonus; supernatural strength and damage are prose. || SKILLS: Language: Ojahee (98%) as Language: Native Tongue 98 (no Ojahee row); Dakir Common (98%) as a Language: Other pick fixed at 98; one language +15 as one Language: Other pick; Basic Radio 45+15; W.P. Energy Rifle; W.P. Axe, which the book says to treat as W.P. Blunt; one W.P. of choice; Hand to Hand: Expert changes to Martial Arts or Assassin for one other skill, no alignment condition printed. || RELATED: seven, plus two at 3 and 5 and one at 8, 10 and 12. Communications +10, Espionage +8, Medical (Paramedic only) +5, Military +10, Pilot +10, Rogue +3 (the Destroyer''s block prints +5 here; the render confirms +3), Science +5, Technical +10, Wilderness +5; Physical any except Prowl (''not possible''); Domestic, Electrical, Mechanical, Pilot Related and W.P. any. Secondary: five, same limits without the bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: ''see weapon systems, plus an energy weapon of choice and 4 E-clips''. The built-in systems are abilities; the energy weapon is a choice from a catalog set. || MONEY: 3000 credits a month plus room, board and bionics, 1000 more a month hazard pay in combat; starts with one month''s pay, stored as 3000."
