## Lore

A minority of Ojahee legionnaires accept partial bionic conversion and become
O''borgs, the Legion''s walking tanks. The Ojahee think of themselves as infantry
first and last and would rather fight inside an armoured body of their own than
ride in one of the tanks other races build, so their regiments field the
O''borgs the way other armies field armoured vehicles.

An O''borg towers about twelve feet tall under grafted armour plate, with a
gatling I-beam gun on one forearm, a particle beam in the chest, missile racks
over the shoulders and a great energy axe for close work. Enough of the
original muscle is left that the strength is still supernatural. The systems
are cruder than a Destroyer''s and carry no stealth gear, force field or
inertial shield, and no O''borg will accept the virtual-reality system, which
Ojahee find offensive. They are front-line fighters and do not need them.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ojahee-borg');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ojahee-borg';

